  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting emergency response to the cholera outbreak</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to reduce mortality and morbidity through rapid intervention in the prevention and treatment of cholera. This UNICEF project provides 1) 500 people with treatment for acute watery diarrhea (incl. cholera), 2) 55,000 people with critical WASH supplies (e.g. WASH/hygiene kits) and 3) 50,000 people with critical cholera kits among other activities. The project provides life-saving assistance to 250,000 people, including 68,850 women, 66,150 men, 115,000 children, and 25,000 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
